WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.150
Game of Thrones is back after the longest
off-season ever, and Episode 1 of Season 7

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.620
sets the stage for the conflicts ahead.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:13.850
Arya is at the Twins, wearing the face of
Walder Frey – who she killed last season.

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:19.350
It’s not clear exactly how the magic of
the Faceless Men works, but by wearing Walder’s

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.120
face, Arya takes his appearance and voice
and everything, and she uses this disguise

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.680
to gather the Freys at a feast.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:31.009
She talks of the Red Wedding, when the Freys
killed Arya’s mother and brother and others.

00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:36.510
And then, with poisoned wine, Arya kills the
Freys, sparing only the women.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:41.820
This revenge was a long time coming, and Arya’s
clearly pleased with her work – but is this

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.530
really justice?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:48.190
The main people behind the Red Wedding – Walder
and Tywin and Roose, and Lothar and Black

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.700
Walder – they’re already dead.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:54.380
Were all these Freys really guilty, and deserving
of death?

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:59.430
There’s a similar thing in the books where
Catelyn is resurrected as Lady Stoneheart,

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:03.870
who mercilessly kills all the Freys she can
find – but it’s not really clear if the

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:09.250
people she kills are all guilty – she even
tries to hang Brienne and Pod.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:13.030
So Stoneheart makes us question whether violent
vengeance is right.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:17.390
And similarly, Arya’s killing is questioned
when she runs into Ed Sheeran and his Lannister

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.390
mates.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:23.170
This is a humanising scene where a bunch of
nameless redshirt soldiers show that they,

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.760
too, have personalities and families and dreams.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:31.770
They are Lannister soldiers, they’ve probably
done bad things – but Arya realises they

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:34.290
still deserve to live.

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:37.320
Maybe the same was true of some of these Freys.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:43.470
Arya’s arc has made her a ruthless killer,
but she’s still capable of mercy and humanity

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:48.140
– and that’s one of the themes of this
episode – justice and vengeance versus mercy

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.190
and compassion.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:55.190
After the intro, a dark fog roll in, with
the Night King and white walkers leading the

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:59.940
army of the dead, which includes a few undead
giants.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.310
This giant is missing an eye so some fans
think it’s the corpse of Wun Wun who died

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:05.530
at Winterfell.

00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:10.759
But Wun Wun lost his right eye – this guy
his left eye – so it must be some other

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:12.440
one-eyed giant.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.920
Twelve-foot-tall zombie giants are pretty
scary, and in the books, there are also undead

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:22.530
bears and birds and “things in the water”,
and “ice spiders”, even rumours of ice

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.530
dragons.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.400
Maybe we’ll see some of these this season.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:29.260
Also, it’s cool to see the darkness brought
by the white walkers.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.569
Cause the walkers aren’t just frosty blokes
who like the cold and the dark, they bring

00:02:33.569 --> 00:02:39.360
the cold and dark, they kinda are the cold
and dark, they are winter.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:42.730
The walkers might be connected to this world’s
irregular seasons.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:47.740
So maybe the seasons will become normal after
the walkers are defeated.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.930
If the walkers are defeated.

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:55.590
One their great opponents is Bran, now called
the three-eyed raven cause he’s got psychic

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:56.840
powers and shit.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:01.230
He arrives at the Wall with Meera Reed, and
Ed of the Night’s Watch lets them through.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.209
Some people thought that this mark that the
Night King made on Bran last season might

00:03:05.209 --> 00:03:10.239
let the white walkers pass through or break
the Wall when Bran enters, but it looks like

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:13.260
the Wall’s still standing – for now.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.280
At Winterfell, King Jon Snow holds a meeting
with the north.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.100
He says they gotta get dragonglass to fight
the white walkers – because dragonglass

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.630
kills white walkers.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:25.850
And he sends Tormund and the wildlings to
defend Eastwatch – one of the castles on

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:26.850
the Wall.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:31.069
For centuries, wildings have attacked the
Wall – but now, with a common enemy, the

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:33.420
wildlings and the north stand together.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:38.390
Jon says that all northerners, including children,
will join in the war against the walkers.

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:42.670
Robett Glover and Lyanna Mormont argue over
whether girls should be allowed to fight,

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:46.239
and it’s decided that children of both sexes
will join in the war.

00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:51.879
It’s crazy how in a world like Westeros,
gender equality can mean conscripting ten-year-old

00:03:51.879 --> 00:03:55.480
girls to fight and die against zombie hordes.

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.819
Jon and Sansa argue over whether the Umber
and Karstark families, whose leaders betrayed

00:03:59.819 --> 00:04:04.550
the Starks for Bolton, should be allowed to
keep their castles, or be replaced.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:09.630
Littlefinger enjoys seeing Sansa and Jon divided
– but Jon decides to keep the old families,

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:12.569
and accept oaths from their new young rulers.

00:04:12.569 --> 00:04:17.510
Alys Karstark has a plot in the books about
Jon helping her deal with her uncle, while

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:21.669
Ned Umber is a character invented for the
show – cool how he has this cross on his

00:04:21.669 --> 00:04:26.919
clothes, though, representing the Umber chains
– the older Umbers wore something similar.

00:04:26.919 --> 00:04:31.770
Sansa and Jon talk afterwards, and basically,
Jon’s a decent ruler, but could benefit

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.099
from Sansa’s advice.

00:04:33.099 --> 00:04:38.479
Over the last six seasons, she’s learned
politics from the best – or, you could say,

00:04:38.479 --> 00:04:39.990
from the worst.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:44.050
Jon mostly learned from his uncle Ned – who
is a great bloke, but lost his head cause

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:48.300
he was too dumb – or too merciful maybe
– to survive.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:51.969
The Starks get a letter from Cersei, who demands
that they come south and kneel.

00:04:51.969 --> 00:04:56.590
There’s a long history of Starks coming
south and dying there – Rickard, Brandon,

00:04:56.590 --> 00:05:01.139
Lya, Ned, Robb – so it’s smart of Jon
and Sansa to stay put.

00:05:01.139 --> 00:05:05.369
Cersei is a problem, but it’s the walkers
who threaten all.

00:05:05.369 --> 00:05:09.330
At the capital, Jaime and Cersei Lannister
chatona map.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:14.129
Cersei talks about how she hates Tyrion – who
she believes killed Joffrey – which he didn’t.

00:05:14.129 --> 00:05:17.520
And that he killed Tywin – which he did.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.279
In the books, there’s a prophecy that Cersei’s
brother will kill her.

00:05:21.279 --> 00:05:25.599
Cersei thinks this means Tyrion, but some
readers think Jaime – go watch that video

00:05:25.599 --> 00:05:31.180
. Cersei also reveals her feelings about her
son Tommen, who committed suicide last season.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.930
It was kinda weird how calm and cold Cersei
was about Tommen’s death.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:40.050
Now we learn that she feels that Tommen betrayed
her, by going over to the Faith.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:45.430
You’d think she’d feel grief that her
son died alone and confused and afraid – but

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:48.789
Cersei hardens her heart against Tommen.

00:05:48.789 --> 00:05:53.759
If this is how she treats her son, just imagine
how she’ll treat her enemies.

00:05:53.759 --> 00:05:57.250
As Jaime points out, things look bad for the
Lannisters – Cersei’s surrounded.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:01.520
Daenerys is invading from the east, with her
allies in Dorne and the Reach.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.249
King Jon’s in the north.

00:06:03.249 --> 00:06:07.759
And with the death of Walder Frey, the Lannisters
have no allies left.

00:06:07.759 --> 00:06:12.649
So Cersei decides to make a new friend – King
Euron Greyjoy.

00:06:12.649 --> 00:06:17.339
Euron sails in to King’s Landing, with his
red eye on the ironborn ships.

00:06:17.339 --> 00:06:20.050
In the books, Euron’s ship is called the
Silence.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:25.039
It’s crewed by “mutes and mongrels”
, painted red to hide the blood – and when

00:06:25.039 --> 00:06:31.309
men see his sails, they pray . In Season 6
of the show, some people felt Euron was kinda

00:06:31.309 --> 00:06:32.339
boring.

00:06:32.339 --> 00:06:35.069
Just another gruff bearded white bloke who
shouts a lot.

00:06:35.069 --> 00:06:40.969
But now, Euron’s different – more expressive
and colourful and nutty – like a peanut

00:06:40.969 --> 00:06:41.969
M&amp;M.

00:06:41.969 --> 00:06:46.469
A bit more like the Euron of the books – though
not as sorcerous or scary.

00:06:46.469 --> 00:06:50.491
Jaime feels insecure that this black-clad
Jack Sparrow is hitting on his sister, so

00:06:50.491 --> 00:06:55.220
he reminds Euron of some old family beef – the
Greyjoy Rebellion.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:59.779
Bout ten years ago, Balon rebelled against
the crown, so the rest of Westeros got together

00:06:59.779 --> 00:07:01.319
and put him down.

00:07:01.319 --> 00:07:05.249
Which was pretty sweet – a young Robert
and Ned and Stannis and Tywin and Barry and

00:07:05.249 --> 00:07:10.029
Thoros and Gregor and Jorah and Jaime all
fought together against the Greyjoys.

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:14.909
The Greyjoys lost of course, but “What is
dead can never die” and now’s Euron back,

00:07:14.909 --> 00:07:18.740
offering his hand – both hands – in marriage
to Cersei.

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:24.200
She says no, but he says he’ll return with
a gift – so what’s he planning?

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:28.599
Cersei did just mention how much she hates
Tyrion, and Tyrion has been offered as a gift

00:07:28.599 --> 00:07:34.270
to a queen before, so maybe Euron has eyes
on the dwarf.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:39.379
In Oldtown, at the Citadel, Sam’s weighing
brains and stacking scrolls and scooping soup

00:07:39.379 --> 00:07:40.809
and scrubbing poop.

00:07:40.809 --> 00:07:44.340
Game of Thrones Hogwarts is not as fun as
he thought it would be.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:48.050
He came here to learn secrets that would help
in the fight against the white walkers, but

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:51.479
no one here seems to believes that they even
exist.

00:07:51.479 --> 00:07:54.860
Archmaester Ebrose assures him that every
other time someone thought the world would

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.490
end, it didn’t.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:00.620
But Sam has seen the threat is real, so he
breaks into the restricted section of the

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:05.599
library, just like Harry Potter, to find something
to help against the walkers.

00:08:05.599 --> 00:08:09.699
This might relate to something that’s happening
in the books, when Jaqen H’ghar breaks into

00:08:09.699 --> 00:08:15.050
the Citadel – go watch that video . But
in the show, Sam gets a book about dragonglass,

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:16.599
the stuff that kills white walkers.

00:08:16.599 --> 00:08:22.039
And he learns of huge caves beneath Dragonstone
full of obsidian – which’ll be super duper

00:08:22.039 --> 00:08:24.150
useful against the white walkers.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:29.259
For the record, Stannis already told Sam about
that dragonglass , but who listens to Stannis,

00:08:29.259 --> 00:08:30.259
right?

00:08:30.259 --> 00:08:33.690
Later, we find Jorah is at the Citadel, suffering
from greyscale.

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:36.750
Dany ordered him to find a cure, remember.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:39.910
And it might just be that the book Sam found
could hold the answer.

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:44.660
This page mentions “dragonglass as a cure”
for “illnesses and dise[ase]”.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:46.880
It mentions “ingestion”.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.990
So maybe eating dragonglass can cure greyscale?

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:56.390
It would be weird if the same stuff that created
white walkers – who can make icy zombies

00:08:56.390 --> 00:09:00.400
– can save people from greyscale – which
makes stone zombies.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:05.280
There’re lots of different types of zombies
in Thrones – maybe they’re all related

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:06.280
somehow.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:10.400
One other thing – this knife on this page
about Valyrian weapons looks just like the

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.440
catspaw’s knife, that Littlefinger used
to frame Tyrion.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.640
The same knife that Arya wears on a magazine
cover.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:21.360
It’s not clear what the point of this will
be – but it sure looks like this dagger

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.360
is important.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:28.200
It’s only Episode 1, and Sam’s already
making discoveries.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:32.410
Back at Winterfell for a moment, Pod gets
his ass beat by Brienne, and Tormund wishes

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:33.570
it was him.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:37.270
Petyr creeps on Sansa, but she swiftly shuts
him down.

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:42.410
Littlefinger used to be an amazing schemer
with a complex plot in the early story – now,

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.870
he mostly hangs around and says snide shit.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:49.280
He’s gonna have to do something if he’s
to survive this season.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:54.930
We then get a scene with the coolest new squad
in the story – Thoros, Beric, and the Hound,

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:56.130
Sandor Clegane.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:59.720
They stay at a farmhouse, and Sandor has been
here before.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:03.770
In Season 4, the Hound and Arya stayed with
a farmer and his daughter here.

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:09.000
Sandor mugged the farmer, said they’d die
by winter, but now when he finds them dead,

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:13.000
he shows regret, and pays his respects by
burying them.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:17.140
The act of gravedigging refers to a bit in
the books where, after his apparent death,

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:22.810
the Hound becomes a monk and digs graves as
penance for his sins – a peaceful end for

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:27.480
the character in the books . In the show,
the Hound’s wars are not over, but the point

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.690
of the gravedigging seems the same.

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:35.420
Sandor used to be a remorseless killer – remember
when he killed that kid Mycah in Season 1?

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:39.050
But now he has some humanity and respect for
life.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:44.180
Back when Sandor hung out with Arya, he was
always the brutal one, while she wanted mercy.

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:50.300
Now it’s the other way round – Arya remorselessly
slaughters, while the Hound mourns the dead.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:53.880
How will these guys get along if they meet
again?

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.920
Sandor Beric and Thoros talk about destiny,
and god.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:02.070
The Hound overcomes his fear of fire and looks
into a flame, seeing a vision of the marching

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:05.640
dead by a castle where “the Wall” meets
the sea.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:09.700
So that’s Eastwatch, where Jon sent the
wildlings – and in the books, Melisandre

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:12.570
does predict that the dead will attack there.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.310
But Sandor also sees “a mountain” that
“Looks like an arrowhead”.

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.960
It’s not clear what this means.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:24.530
The mountain could mean a place like the Fist
of the First Men, or the obsidian at Dragonstone

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:29.650
, or a symbolic mountain like the Hound’s
brother Gregor, or a zombie giant maybe.

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:33.110
And the arrowhead bit could mean dragonglass
arrowheads, maybe?

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.120
It’s hard to say.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:40.560
But one thing is clear – the dead are marching
on Eastwatch.

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:44.940
The final scene is something that readers
have waited for for decades.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:50.170
Twenty years ago, the first book came out,
and ever since fans have hoped to see Daenerys

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.170
arrive at Dragonstone.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:56.980
Her home, where she was born, where her ancestors
the dragonlords lived for centuries – and

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:00.750
the starting point for her campaign to take
the Throne.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:05.000
There is a sweet seat, and Stannis’ banner,
and sand is rough and course, and it kinda

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.670
makes no sense that the castle is empty.

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:12.550
But the significance of this scene is as the
beginning of the end, the start of the final

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:16.120
act in the story of Game of Thrones.

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:17.230
Thanks for watching.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:20.610
Subscribe for a new video for each episode
every week.

